Derived algorithms — credited, independently implemented
--------------------------------------------------------

  src/d3d/d3d8_swizzle.h
    Implements Xbox Z-order (Morton) texture unswizzling. The
    masked-increment technique is Fabian Giesen's, published on his blog;
    xemu's hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/swizzle.c is cited in the file as the
    reference that pointed us at it.

  src/d3d/d3d8_combiners.h
    NV2A register-combiner translation. Cites xemu's pgraph combiner
    implementation as a reference for the hardware's behaviour.

  src/apu/apu_lowpass.h  (branch option-c)
    The voice processor's per-voice low-pass: Hal Chamberlin's digital state
    variable filter ("Musical Applications of Microprocessors", 2nd ed.,
    1985), written from the book. It replaces the filter that came from
    xemu's hw/xbox/mcpx/apu/vp/svf.h (GPLv2), which is no longer in the tree,
    together with the unused DSP56300 core/DMA declarations from xemu's
    GPL-2.0-or-later DSP headers. The input level sqrt(q/2 + 0.01) keeps the
    loudness the old filter gave. Takedawn's xboxrecomp fork made the same
    replacement first (its own MIT apu_lowpass.h); the idea is credited to
    it, the code here is this tree's. tests/apu_lowpass compares the new
    filter with stored outputs of the old one (tolerance in the test).

  src/nv2a_gl/gl_vsh.c nv2a_ptsize, gl_vsh_ff.c, gl_psh.c u_psprite  (branch option-c)
    Point size and point sprites: SET_POINT_SIZE, the SET_POINT_PARAMS
    distance attenuation and SET_POINT_SMOOTH_ENABLE as the texture stage 3
    point coordinate, after the hardware model in xemu's
    hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/glsl/vsh-ff.c, vsh.c and psh.c (LGPL-2.1-or-later),
    written for this tree's shaders, not copied.

